 {"decision_id": "D-035", "date": "2026-07-21", "decision": "EXTENDED v2.1 BUILT AND FULLY PROVEN (staged, pre-deploy report issued): compound tp-N-sl-entry, HOLD_LEG_SELECTIVE (wire-resolved vs campaign direction, else fail-closed), informational notes (TP_LEVEL_NOTE/TP_HIT_NOTE - recorded, NEVER engine instructions), PER-CLAUSE COMPLETENESS hard fail-closed (category-coverage; one whitelisted temporal idiom 'market close'). Proofs: failing-first 4 RED -> 44/44 GREEN; v2.0->v2.1 byte-identity 33/35 with changes EXACTLY [45937, 45940] (the D-028 defect messages - intended, asserted); byte-identity gate caught a REAL regression during build (45885 close-100% tripped percent-coverage - EXPLICIT_FULL_EXIT added to covering set); battery 9/9 suites 357 checks; full replay: ENTRY->non-ENTRY 0 (halt clean), M->E 112, OTHER->MANAGEMENT 85 (new typed notes), M->REVIEW 50 (silent-partials now loud - intended class), 240-recon in results JSON with all non-ENTRY named. WIRE_NOMINAL_OPEN RECOMMENDATION: option (3) accept proximity window with stated residual risk NOW (L20/L50 records carry no wire-consumable setup linkage, so option-1 alignment needs a defined terminal-marker shape = scoped future change; retro-adjudication correctly BLOCKED by governance precondition (c) - no named defect); residual risk = two genuine campaigns within 18h; forward-mitigated because v2.1-era campaigns terminate via instruction tokens or F006-style adjudications. DIRECTIONAL-A: first fire captured 06:39:00Z 'Farouks Playbook: Bullish Engulfing' - LIVE013 capturing successfully. Deploy staged, awaiting go: copy v2 files -> restart wire/watcher/observer -> F006-scoped verify + ledger byte-identity -> amend D-018.", "authority": "research/farouk_pilot/always_on_tradingview_receiver_plan/stage_c_tooling/farouk_plus/parser_replay/v2_reproof_results.json", "hash": "see file"},
